---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="DZ: The Writer — Dmitrii Zhukov">
  <section class="px-6 pt-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-5">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-4">CH 01</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-6xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-tight md:text-7xl">DZ: The Writer</h1>
        </div>
        <a href="/cv/dmitrii-zhukov-cv.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="cv-btn">&#8595; Download CV</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-ink-dim">
        Game writing • Narrative design • Worldbuilding • Branching dialogue • 
        Character & dialogue writing • Mystery storytelling • Environmental storytelling • 
        Published novelist • Cross-functional collaboration
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[250px_1fr]">
        <div class="space-y-6">
        <img
          src="/writer/dz-1.webp"
          alt="Dmitrii Zhukov — Writer"
          class="aspect-[3.5/4] w-full border border-line object-cover"
        />
        
        <aside class="space-y-5 font-mono text-sm">
            <div>
              <p class="mb-1 uppercase tracking-widest text-violet">Status</p>
              <p class="text-ink-dim">· Open to junior and mid-level game narrative roles</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="mb-1 uppercase tracking-widest text-violet">Toolkit</p>
              <p class="text-ink-dim">· articy:draft · Twine · Confluence · Notion · Figma · Photoshop · Markdown · MDX · Jira · Git · AI-assisted writing workflows </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="mb-1 uppercase tracking-widest text-violet">Languages</p>
              <p class="text-ink-dim">· English (advanced)<br />· Russian (native)<br />· Ukrainian (advanced)<br />· German (intermediate)<br />· Serbian (beginner)</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="mb-1 uppercase tracking-widest text-violet">Based in</p>
              <p class="text-ink-dim">· Belgrade, Serbia<br />· Open to relocation</p>
            </div>
          </aside>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-lg text-ink-dim">
          <div>
            <p class="placeholder block"><span class="font-bold text-violet">[Bio]: </span>My name is Dmitrii Zhukov. 
            I am a game narrative designer and a published novelist. I build mystery-driven 
            worlds and atmospheric horror. I create stories that ask the player to investigate 
            the mysteries and make uneasy choices.
            <br/>
            <br/>
            My first published novel, <i>Myst</i>, became the foundation for  
            <span class="font-bold text-violet-bright"> STATIC</span>, a game concept that 
            reimagines its story as a third-person mystery-horror adventure. This site is
            a presentation of that concept: the dialogue engine, the lore artifacts, the case files, and 
            the documents.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="placeholder block"><span class="font-bold text-violet">[Career]: </span>Before narrative design, 
            I spent years in fintech as a Senior Technical Writer and Product Documentation 
            Manager, owning documentation ecosystems end-to-end and working daily with 
            engineering, QA, and support teams. Structuring complex information, keeping a 
            hundred moving parts consistent, writing for a reader who is lost and needs to
            find their way — these are the same skills narrative systems are built with.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="placeholder block"><span class="font-bold text-violet">[Game writing]: </span>Writing has been 
            the core of my working life at every scale, from support instructions to 
            leading a documentation team. Fiction has run alongside it the whole way.
            <br/>
            <br/>
            <span class="font-bold text-violet-bright"> STATIC</span> is where the two finally meet: systems thinking from one 
            career, storytelling from the other. Narrative design is where they stop being 
            separate careers at all.</p>
          </div>
      </div>
    </div>

      <hr class="rule my-12" />
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl uppercase tracking-tight text-ink">Influences</h2>
      <p class="note mt-1 inline-block">
        
        The stories I invent are shaped by curiosity and observation as much as by fiction.
        Inspiration comes from literature, cinema, video games, music, traveling, education. Visiting 
        old castle ruins, listening to a history lecture, or hearing a clever turn of phrase 
        in a song lyric often sparks new ideas: worlds, places, characters, narrative threads. 
        I constantly collect fragments (atmosphere, dialogue pieces, symbolism, plot twists) and 
        then reinterpret them into something new.<br /><br />

        <span class="font-bold text-violet">• Games:</span> Bloodborne, Control, Alan Wake, The Last of Us, Hellblade: Senua's Sacrifice, Death Stranding.<br /><br />
        
        <span class="font-bold text-violet">• Films:</span> Drive, It Follows, Se7en, Arrival, Memento, Blade Runner 2049.<br /><br />
        
        <span class="font-bold text-violet">• Books:</span> One Hundred Years of Solitude, Blood Meridian, Drood, Harry Potter, Ring, The Langoliers.<br /><br />
        
        <span class="font-bold text-violet">• Music:</span> Poets of the Fall, STARSET, The Midnight, The National, Oh Hiroshima, Taylor Swift. <br /><br />
        
        Every place I visit and every person I meet has a story waiting to be uncovered.

      </p>
      
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
